block: mq-deadline: do not merge in front of a request

front_merges off by default. Looking for a request to glue the new one
in front of costs a search on every submission and pays only when a
process writes backwards through a file, which is rare. Sequential
throughput may drop; that is what has to be measured.

From XanMod's 7.0 series.

--- a/block/mq-deadline.c
+++ b/block/mq-deadline.c
@@ -549,7 +549,7 @@
 	dd->fifo_expire[DD_READ] = read_expire;
 	dd->fifo_expire[DD_WRITE] = write_expire;
 	dd->writes_starved = writes_starved;
-	dd->front_merges = 1;
+	dd->front_merges = 0;
 	dd->last_dir = DD_WRITE;
 	dd->fifo_batch = fifo_batch;
 	dd->prio_aging_expire = prio_aging_expire;
